solution:
The Arrhenius equation, Eq. (6.18), is

\(k = \mathrm{A}\,e^{-E_a/RT}\)

where

- \(k\) is the rate constant of the reaction;
- \(E_a\) is the activation energy;
- \(R\) is the molar gas constant, \(8.314\ \mathrm{J\ K^{-1}\ mol^{-1}}\);
- \(T\) is the temperature in kelvin;
- \(\mathrm{A}\) is the pre-exponential factor, which the chapter notes is related to the frequency of collisions and which for a first order reaction has the same unit as \(k\).
